---
title: input_validation (EIP-7951)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> q_check_len : receive raw input bytes
    q_check_len --> q_check_r : input_length == 160
    q_check_len --> q_fail : input_length != 160
    q_check_r --> q_check_s : 0 < r < n
    q_check_r --> q_fail : r <= 0 OR r >= n
    q_check_s --> q_check_qx : 0 < s < n
    q_check_s --> q_fail : s <= 0 OR s >= n
    q_check_qx --> q_check_qy : 0 <= qx < p
    q_check_qx --> q_fail : qx >= p
    q_check_qy --> q_check_curve : 0 <= qy < p
    q_check_qy --> q_fail : qy >= p
    q_check_curve --> q_check_inf : qy^2 == qx^3 + a*qx + b (mod p)
    q_check_curve --> q_fail : point not on curve
    q_check_inf --> q_valid : (qx, qy) != (0, 0)
    q_check_inf --> q_fail : point is infinity
    q_valid --> [*] : validation passed
    q_fail --> [*] : return empty

    note right of q_check_r
        INV-005: All 5 validation checks MUST be performed in order
        INV-006: Any single validation failure returns empty immediately
    end note

    note right of q_check_s
        INV-007: r and s are strictly bounded (0, n) - exclusive
        INV-008: qx and qy are bounded [0, p) - inclusive of zero
    end note
